      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "was exceeded only once out of 482 planning intervals. Thus,",
      "bbox": [
        48.9639892578125,
        689.6363525390625,
        300.021484375,
        698.5429077148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the estimates were bounded accurately in around 99.8% of",
      "bbox": [
        48.9639892578125,
        701.5913696289062,
        300.0214538574219,
        710.4979248046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "planning intervals, well within the 95% confidence bound (Fig",
      "bbox": [
        48.9639892578125,
        713.54638671875,
        300.02142333984375,
        722.4529418945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6d).",
      "bbox": [
        48.9639892578125,
        725.5013427734375,
        64.73478698730469,
        734.4078979492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We demonstrate a quantitative difference in the observance",
      "bbox": [
        58.9269905090332,
        739.1283569335938,
        300.0219421386719,
        748.034912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 7. Rallycar dynamics noise model",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        177.09925842285156,
        441.6196594238281,
        184.2245330810547
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the PAC Bounds in Figure 6. When optimizing the bounds",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        190.42535400390625,
        563.0354614257812,
        199.3319091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with the nominal dynamics, the probability of collision esti-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        202.38037109375,
        563.035400390625,
        211.28692626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mates were only bounded in 93.9% of planning intervals (Fig",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        214.33538818359375,
        563.035400390625,
        223.241943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6b). This decrease in bound accuracy is even more apparent",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        226.2904052734375,
        563.0355834960938,
        235.19696044921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "when running the controller without feedback to compensate",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        238.24639892578125,
        563.035400390625,
        247.1529541015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for unmodeled noise, resulting in only 64.7% of planning",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        250.201416015625,
        563.0355224609375,
        259.10797119140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "intervals having bounded probability of collision estimates",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        262.15643310546875,
        563.0352783203125,
        271.06298828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(Fig 6a).",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        274.1114196777344,
        347.2854309082031,
        283.0179748535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "VI. HARDWARE EXPERIMENTS",
      "bbox": [
        370.8919982910156,
        300.6064147949219,
        504.1256408691406,
        309.5129699707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A. Rally Car",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        316.55908203125,
        365.55682373046875,
        325.1468505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1) Hardware: To evaluate our method on physical hard-",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399719238281,
        332.01141357421875,
        563.039794921875,
        340.91796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ware, we ran PAC-NMPC on a 1/10th-scale Traxxas Rally",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        343.9664001464844,
        563.0354614257812,
        352.8729553222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Car platform. The algorithm runs on a Nvidia Jetson Orin",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        355.92138671875,
        563.035400390625,
        364.82794189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mounted on the bottom platform. The control interface is a",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        367.87738037109375,
        563.0353393554688,
        376.783935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "variable electronic speed controller (VESC), which executes",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        379.8323669433594,
        563.0355834960938,
        388.7389221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "commands and provides servo state information. The position",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        391.787353515625,
        563.0354614257812,
        400.69390869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and orientation is tracked with an OptiTrack system.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        403.7423400878906,
        527.6880493164062,
        412.6488952636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2) Setup:",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399719238281,
        415.9800109863281,
        360.67449951171875,
        424.5677795410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The route, virtual obstacle placements, and",
      "bbox": [
        369.31695556640625,
        415.8903503417969,
        563.0397338867188,
        424.7969055175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "TVLQR costs are identical to those in the simulation exper-",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        427.8453369140625,
        563.0354614257812,
        436.75189208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "iments. We optimize a 12 timestep trajectory with ∆t = 0.1",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        439.64093017578125,
        563.0362548828125,
        448.7068786621094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sec at a replanning period of H = 0.2 sec. We apply a",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        451.5959167480469,
        563.0360717773438,
        460.661865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quadratic cost to the final state of the trajectory: J(τ) =",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        463.5509033203125,
        563.035400390625,
        472.6168518066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xNT +1QfxNT +1 where Qf = diag([1.0, 1.0, 0.4, 0.1, 0.0]).",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        475.50689697265625,
        563.03662109375,
        486.26983642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Parameters were L = 2, M = 1024, δ = 0.05, γ = 10.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        487.4618835449219,
        536.6085815429688,
        496.52783203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We model the rally car dynamics as a stochastic bicycle",
      "bbox": [
        321.93994140625,
        499.70428466796875,
        563.0348510742188,
        508.61083984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model where noise is modeled as a 3 component Gaussian",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        511.6593017578125,
        563.0355224609375,
        520.5658569335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mixture Model. This mixture model was fit from 2500 samples",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        523.615234375,
        563.0353393554688,
        532.5217895507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of data collected with the car (Fig. 7). We perform the same",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        535.5702514648438,
        563.035400390625,
        544.476806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ablation study as done in the simulation experiments.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        547.5252685546875,
        530.7763671875,
        556.4318237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3) Results: PAC-NMPC ran onboard the rally car in real-",
      "bbox": [
        321.93994140625,
        559.6722412109375,
        563.0347900390625,
        568.5787963867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "time and followed the path while avoiding nearby obstacles. In",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        571.6282958984375,
        563.035400390625,
        580.5348510742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 8, we display the path taken by the car with collisions",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        583.583251953125,
        563.0353393554688,
        592.4898071289062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "annotated by arrows. During each planning interval of H =",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        595.3788452148438,
        563.037841796875,
        604.44482421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0.2 sec, the controller achieved an average of 10 iterations of",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        607.3338623046875,
        563.0387573242188,
        616.3998413085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "trajectory distribution optimization with approximately 20ms",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        619.4482421875,
        563.03515625,
        628.3547973632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "per iteration.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        631.4032592773438,
        363.8829650878906,
        640.309814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The controller consistently produced PAC bounds ≤10%",
      "bbox": [
        321.93988037109375,
        642.77001953125,
        563.036376953125,
        652.3938598632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "probability of collision, which accurately bounded the Monte",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        655.4422607421875,
        563.0353393554688,
        664.3488159179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Carlo estimates of the probability of collision at all planning",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        667.3972778320312,
        563.0352783203125,
        676.3038330078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "intervals (Fig. 9d). In this context, Monte Carlo estimates",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        679.352294921875,
        563.0352783203125,
        688.2588500976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "refer to sampled trajectories using the simulated stochastic",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        691.3082885742188,
        563.035400390625,
        700.21484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics model. When optimizing with stochastic dynamics",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        703.2633056640625,
        563.035400390625,
        712.1698608398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and without feedback, the car collided with virtual obstacles",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        715.21826171875,
        563.0352172851562,
        724.1248168945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "twice, likely due to unmodeled dynamics not captured in the",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        727.1732788085938,
        563.0353393554688,
        736.079833984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gaussian mixture model (Fig. 9c). When optimizing the bound",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        739.1282958984375,
        563.0355224609375,
        748.0348510742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
